@base = http://localhost:3000
@cookie = repodesk_session=REPLACE_WITH_SESSION
@csrf = REPLACE_WITH_CSRF
@workspace = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### Read redacted settings (workspace deployment operator)
GET {{base}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/search-console
Cookie: {{cookie}}

### Save a JSON key. Use the latest revision from GET; this clears properties and disables.
# Paste the real escaped JSON through the panel, not into version-controlled files.
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/search-console
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Origin: {{base}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"revision": 0, "settings": {"enabled": false, "siteUrls": []}, "serviceAccount": "REPLACE_WITH_ESCAPED_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON"}

### Discover properties. Add the service account email as a Search Console user first.
POST {{base}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/search-console/properties
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Origin: {{base}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"revision": 1}

### Select exact returned property identifiers and enable; Google access is verified.
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/search-console
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Origin: {{base}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"revision": 1, "settings": {"enabled": true, "siteUrls": ["sc-domain:example.com"]}}

### Remove the local credential and disable. Revoke the remote key in Google Cloud separately.
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/workspaces/{{workspace}}/plugins/search-console
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Origin: {{base}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"revision": 2, "settings": {"enabled": false, "siteUrls": []}, "removeCredential": true}

### Telegram private chat examples (active workspace member)
# List the Search Console properties available to this workspace.
# Show clicks, impressions, CTR and average position for example.com during September 2026.
# Show the top search queries for sc-domain:example.com from 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-07.
# List sitemaps for example.com.
# Inspect Google's indexed version of https://example.com/blog/intro.
